---
import ArchitecturePage from '../../components/ArchitecturePage.astro';
import cadThinking from '../../data/architecture/cad-agent-thinking.json';

const visibleSignals = [
	'The claimed job, its structured goal, and its high-level plan (checkpointed before the loop starts)',
	'The active step, the tool calls requested for it, and their results (that step\'s observations)',
	'Every model turn\'s raw request and response, correlated by agent_turn and step_turn',
	'Step transitions (pending → in_progress → completed) and the loop\'s terminal outcome',
	'Validation, commit, reindex, and export results, and any non-fatal warnings',
];

const protectedSignals = [
	'Hidden token-by-token model deliberation or private chain of thought (the Responses API does not expose it)',
	'Prompt text and complete source bodies are never sent to clients — only milestone events are',
	'Credentials, storage paths, or database access — the model never receives them',
];

const toolGroups = [
	{
		domain: 'index (read-only)',
		note: 'Also the only two tools PlanningAgent may call while building the high-level plan.',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'index_search', mutating: false, params: 'query: str (1–1000, required) · limit: int (1–10, required)', summary: 'Search semantic CAD features in the selected part by free-text query; returns ranked matches with semantic IDs and scores.' },
			{ name: 'index_get_feature', mutating: false, params: 'semantic_id: str (required)', summary: 'Retrieve one feature\'s exact role, parameters, dependencies, and dependents by exact semantic ID.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'feature',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'create_feature', mutating: true, params: 'semantic_id, function_name, role, docstring, function_body: str (required) · parameters, dependencies, search_keys: list (optional)', summary: 'Create one new, isolated semantic CadQuery feature function in the candidate. Does not wire it into build_model.' },
			{ name: 'edit_feature', mutating: true, params: 'semantic_id?, function_name?: str (≥1 required to identify target) · role?, parameters?, dependencies?, search_keys?, docstring?, function_body?: optional replacements', summary: 'Change one or more properties of an existing feature; only fields you pass are changed. Does not rename or touch build_model.' },
			{ name: 'delete_feature', mutating: true, params: 'semantic_id?, function_name?: str (≥1 required)', summary: 'Delete an existing agent-created feature. Refuses if still referenced by another feature\'s dependencies or by build_model.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'parameter',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'create_parameter', mutating: true, params: 'parameter_name: str (required) · value: float (> 0, required)', summary: 'Add one new agent-owned ModelParams field with a numeric default.' },
			{ name: 'edit_parameter', mutating: true, params: 'parameter_name: str (required) · value: float (> 0, required)', summary: 'Change an existing ModelParams field\'s default value (any field, agent-created or hand-authored). Never renames.' },
			{ name: 'delete_parameter', mutating: true, params: 'parameter_name: str (required)', summary: 'Delete an existing agent-created ModelParams field. Refuses if still referenced by any feature.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'build_model',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'edit_cad_build_model', mutating: true, params: 'function_body: str (1–8000 chars, required)', summary: 'Replace the entire body of build_model, the final assembly-wiring step. Rejects wiring in a function that doesn\'t exist yet in the candidate.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'part',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'create_cad_part', mutating: true, params: 'part_name: str (required, must be unique in the project)', summary: 'Create one new CAD part with a minimal, valid, empty model.py skeleton. Does not create parameters or features.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'geometry',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'check_geometry', mutating: false, params: 'none — all identity comes from the run\'s ToolExecutionContext', summary: 'Inspect the candidate\'s actual executed geometry (volume, bounding box, center of mass, solid/face/edge counts, the largest planar faces with their angle from horizontal, and a sharp-edge count) against the immediately preceding candidate. Deterministic evidence only — never modifies source, never gates anything.' },
		],
	},
	{
		domain: 'step',
		tools: [
			{ name: 'request_step_completion', mutating: false, params: 'summary: str (1–2000, required)', summary: 'Signal that the active plan step is complete. The orchestrator gates this — see the Completion Gate stage — it is not honored blindly.' },
		],
	},
];
---

<ArchitecturePage
	title="Agent 3D Reasoning Loop"
	summary="An auditable view of the actual Agent3D loop: one model call per turn, a bounded tool catalog, an orchestrator that executes and gates every decision, and a commit pipeline that only starts once the plan is done."
	section="Reasoning view"
	active="cad-thinking"
	document={cadThinking}
	fallback="Loading the Agent 3D reasoning diagram…"
	showExampleNotice={false}
	diagramFirst={true}
	sidebarNote="Production reasoning view: the plan-driven turn loop, its completion gate and turn caps, and the full registered tool catalog."
>
	<h2>What "thinking" means here</h2>
	<p>This page visualizes the system's inspectable decision loop, not a private chain-of-thought transcript. Each numbered card is an implementation-backed stage in <code>workers/agent_3d/agent_3d.py</code> and <code>orchestrator.py</code>. Select a card or connector to inspect its inputs, decisions, guarantees, failure behavior, and source evidence. The loop is genuinely a loop — follow the "another turn" and "step completed, advance" edges back from stage 9 to stages 6 and 5.</p>

	<h2>The shape of one turn</h2>
	<p><code>Agent3D.decide()</code> holds no state between calls. Every turn it rebuilds the same bounded context from scratch — goal and plan in full, the one active step, that step's accumulated observations, and at most 8 recent conversation messages — makes exactly one model call, and returns the raw response unchanged. It never executes what it decides. The orchestrator does: it runs every requested tool call against the edit-scoped candidate, appends the results as observations, and decides whether the loop continues, advances, or ends.</p>

	<h2>What operators can observe</h2>
	<ul>
		{visibleSignals.map((signal) => <li>{signal}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<h2>What the trace intentionally excludes</h2>
	<ul>
		{protectedSignals.map((signal) => <li>{signal}</li>)}
	</ul>

	<h2>Registered tools available to Agent3D</h2>
	<p>All 12 tools below share one <code>ToolRegistry</code> and are available in Agent3D's full mutation-loop catalog. <code>PlanningAgent</code> — the earlier, separate stage that builds the high-level plan — can call only the two read-only <code>index</code> tools; every mutating tool exists only inside the loop this page visualizes. Every tool inherits the same strict contract (<code>base.py</code>): no extra input fields, no type coercion, immutable validated input, and a shared <code>{'{ok, data}'}</code> / <code>{'{ok, error}'}</code> result envelope.</p>
	{toolGroups.map((group) => (
		<div class="tool-group">
			<h3><code>{group.domain}</code>{group.note ? <span class="tool-group__note"> — {group.note}</span> : null}</h3>
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Tool</th>
						<th scope="col">Kind</th>
						<th scope="col">Parameters</th>
						<th scope="col">Summary</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{group.tools.map((tool) => (
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>{tool.name}</code></th>
							<td>{tool.mutating ? 'Mutates candidate' : 'Read-only'}</td>
							<td><code>{tool.params}</code></td>
							<td>{tool.summary}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	))}

	<h3>System actions that are not model tools</h3>
	<p>Goal creation, plan creation, step selection and status transitions, the completion gate, candidate bootstrap, validation queuing, canonical commit, rollback, reindexing, export queueing, and trace logging all remain orchestrator- or worker-owned actions. Agent3D can neither invoke them directly nor bypass their checks — it can only request tool calls from the 12-tool catalog above.</p>

	<h2>Reading the completion gate</h2>
	<p>When the active step addresses a <code>required</code> goal criterion, <code>request_step_completion</code> is checked against one concrete signal: does the candidate have at least one <code>@cad_part</code> feature yet? If not, the call is rejected with <code>STEP_REQUIRES_A_FEATURE</code> and fed back as an observation — not silently honored. The check only looks at feature presence, not full model-parameter wiring, and it is self-limiting: once any feature exists anywhere in the candidate, later steps are never blocked by it, including the step that created that first feature. A step addressing only <code>preserve</code> criteria is never gated at all.</p>

	<h2>Reading the turn caps</h2>
	<p>Two bounds keep a stuck loop from running forever: at most <strong>10 turns</strong> on a single step (<code>AGENT_STEP_TURN_LIMIT</code>) and <strong>24 turns</strong> total (<code>AGENT_TURN_LIMIT</code>). A decision containing no tool call at all fails immediately with <code>AGENT_NO_ACTION</code> rather than silently burning the remaining budget or assuming the step finished. Any of these three outcomes ends the job before the commit pipeline (stages 10–14) is ever reached — nothing partial gets committed.</p>
</ArchitecturePage>
